cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Transcriptomic analyses in neurodevelopment — a two-hour
  tutorial with continuous assessment
message: >-
  If you reuse or adapt this teaching material, please cite it
  using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Adrien
    family-names: Dufour
    email: adrien.dufour@inserm.fr
    affiliation: Inserm
repository-code: https://github.com/adrdufour/M2BD-transcriptomics
abstract: >-
  A two-hour session for M2 Brain Disorders students covering bulk
  RNA-seq, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, with a graded
  practical in Google Colab. Three simulated datasets are generated
  from one shared cell-type expression profile matrix, so that the
  bulk signal is genuinely a mixture of the single-cell reference and
  deconvolution can be taught and assessed with real evidence rather
  than by assertion. Includes the notebook, the datasets, a printable
  figure handout and the generator.
keywords:
  - transcriptomics
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - deconvolution
  - neurodevelopment
  - teaching
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-04'
